  "notes": [
    {
      "id": "curious-world:note:start",
      "title": "Start curious",
      "chapters": [
        {
          "id": "curious-world:chapter:learning",
          "title": "Learn, then retrieve",
          "text": "Read actively, then put the material away and try to retrieve the answer. Retrieval is the useful part of a drill: it shows you what you can recall without a prompt.\n\nDo not worry about perfect first attempts. A miss is a useful signal for what to practise next."
        },
        {
          "id": "curious-world:chapter:connections",
          "title": "Make connections",
          "text": "Facts become easier to remember when they connect to something else. Picture Cairo on the Nile, or connect the rings of Saturn with an image you have seen.\n\nUse the study notes to build context and the drills to make the details stick."
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
